```python
# 5. Parse the response as JSON before accessing its fields
import requests

response = requests.get(
    "https://api.coingecko.com/api/v3/simple/price",
    params={"ids": "dogecoin", "vs_currencies": "inr"}
)
data = response.json()
print(data["dogecoin"]["inr"])
```

The bug was treating the `Response` object like a dictionary. Calling `.json()` parses the response body into a Python dictionary first.